# Colophon — project.done

Completed: 2026-09-15 (THE FINAL BLITZ).

## What shipped

The final audit's ranked list, executed top-down, plus every gate
answer Brandon gave during the blitz:

- **v2.4.1, the hardening release.** The corrupt-database timestamp
  panic guard (events bound once in load_snapshot), staged imports
  validated by a full load before promote (with the end-to-end
  promote-refuses test; rusqlite as an approved dev-dependency), the
  year-heatmap tooltip books count, off-main-thread source-path
  probes, day-start-aware read-through dates, and the false F8
  shortcuts row dropped. Under it: the ten-site D1 comment-drift
  family synced, the D1 rescale SQL deduplicated into one body, the
  CLAUDE.md sync (word-count GO, app-id decision, 6e remainder, house
  file pointer), the spec/README/RESEARCH truth fixes, the em-dash
  sweep across the working document set, MSRV 1.85, SHA-pinned CI on
  a versioned Fedora 44 container, the cargo-deny advisory gate,
  SECURITY.md, dependabot (actions-only), a justfile, .gitattributes,
  the recorded no-pin toolchain decision, and the approved removals
  (scan_sidecars, all_events; rescaled_events kept and marked
  baseline-only; DBusActivatable dropped).
- **v2.5.0, the feature train.** The year heatmap's year pager
  (replacing the silent 52-week rolling window), the per-year recap
  variant, and the cross-book annotation browser.
- **v2.6.0, the word-count axis.** EPUBs provisioned on the sidecar
  pattern (explicit path, partial-MD5 verified, cached, origin
  remembered for auto-pull), words in book / words read / true WPM on
  the book page, lifetime words and the length distribution on the
  overview, and the Length and Pace personality traits. The granted
  zip dependency rides with its vendored crates.
- **GitHub side.** Releases created for v2.2.0 through v2.4.0, the
  truncated description replaced (319 chars), topics swapped, and
  release.yml cutting Releases from tags automatically (proven on
  v2.5.0 and v2.6.0). The social preview is composed from logo.svg at
  ~/Pictures/colophon-social-preview.png for a one-drag manual upload
  (GitHub has no API for it).
- The live sample was refreshed from the device (Brandon mounted the
  Kindle), which surfaced KOReader's cached-total drift (23 s on
  Jingo), recorded as a dated RESEARCH amendment.

Suite 134 tests green (+1 ignored perf harness); clippy -D warnings,
fmt clean, CI (fmt/clippy/advisories/test) green on every pushed
commit. Tags v2.4.1/v2.5.0/v2.6.0 cut verbatim from their patchnotes
entries and verified with git cat-file before pushing.

